1
00:00:00,140 --> 00:00:06,200
Colonel Wilkerson, any thoughts on how our policy toward Israel does or does not benefit the United States?

2
00:00:06,380 --> 00:00:07,640
Another great question.

3
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:13,460
Israel is probably a strategic liability of the first order for the United States.

4
00:00:13,980 --> 00:00:20,500
I'm hoping that getting rid of Netanyahu and at the same time getting rid of Kushner and Pompeo and Trump

5
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:26,060
will alleviate the situation to the extent that we'll get a government in Israel,

6
00:00:26,060 --> 00:00:30,980
maybe, that will see how dangerous it's future.

7
00:00:31,040 --> 00:00:34,280
I said the other day Israel would not be a state in 20 years.

8
00:00:34,380 --> 00:00:34,800
It'd be gone.

9
00:00:35,700 --> 00:00:37,520
It certainly will not be a democracy.

10
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:44,720
It'll be an apartheid state and the world will just reject it as they did South Africa.

11
00:00:45,140 --> 00:00:47,800
But I'm now saying it probably won't be a state.

12
00:00:47,900 --> 00:00:48,460
It'll be gone.

13
00:00:49,780 --> 00:00:53,580
Go back and read the report of the Joint Chiefs of Staff

14
00:00:53,580 --> 00:00:58,500
when Truman was trying to decide whether or not to recognize Israel in 1947-48

15
00:00:58,500 --> 00:01:01,060
and what to do about U.S. policy.

16
00:01:02,460 --> 00:01:06,460
Completely no came from the Joint Chiefs of Staff.

17
00:01:07,440 --> 00:01:11,720
Based on the fact there were 400 some odd million Arabs

18
00:01:11,720 --> 00:01:17,540
and about at that time three, maybe four million Israelis and other things too.

19
00:01:17,540 --> 00:01:20,520
And God, how prescient that report was.

20
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:22,220
Well, it's come true.

21
00:01:22,220 --> 00:01:24,800
They are a strategic liability now.

22
00:01:25,320 --> 00:01:30,480
The only strategic positive with regard to Israel is our relationship.

23
00:01:30,840 --> 00:01:33,380
That is to say, there are a lot of American Jews

24
00:01:33,380 --> 00:01:36,620
and there are a lot of connections with Israel.

25
00:01:36,980 --> 00:01:40,040
That's the only positive aspect to our relationship.

26
00:01:40,280 --> 00:01:41,280
Everything else is negative.

27
00:01:42,240 --> 00:01:45,060
And if you want to go the full Monty,

28
00:01:45,060 --> 00:01:49,140
you could say Israel is the most likely state in the world

29
00:01:49,140 --> 00:01:51,480
to take the United States to Armageddon.

30
00:01:52,240 --> 00:01:55,080
And I could paint you all sorts of ways we would do that

31
00:01:55,080 --> 00:01:56,220
and the ways we would get there.

32
00:01:56,280 --> 00:01:59,020
One would be the fact that for 40 plus years,

33
00:01:59,120 --> 00:02:02,360
the military said, don't ever tell us to put a base in Israel.

34
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:04,220
Don't ever tell us that.

35
00:02:04,320 --> 00:02:05,880
We will not comply.

36
00:02:05,880 --> 00:02:08,120
Well, we just put a base in Israel.

37
00:02:08,900 --> 00:02:11,820
There is a base in Israel flying the stars and stripes now.

38
00:02:12,860 --> 00:02:14,560
In for penny, in for a pound.

39
00:02:14,800 --> 00:02:16,920
Hezbollah shoots a rocket, hits that base.

40
00:02:17,080 --> 00:02:17,540
Guess what?

41
00:02:17,620 --> 00:02:21,660
The United States is with Israel when it goes to war with all of those Arabs

42
00:02:21,660 --> 00:02:23,840
and maybe half the world combined.

43
00:02:23,840 --> 00:02:25,360
Not a good deal.

44
00:02:25,880 --> 00:02:26,860
Not a good deal.

45
00:02:27,240 --> 00:02:30,880
So yes, Israel, I think, needs to be reined in

46
00:02:30,880 --> 00:02:34,020
and it needs to be told in no uncertain terms,

47
00:02:34,140 --> 00:02:38,000
you will change and you will change swiftly and effectively

48
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:41,740
or you can count your sugar daddy gone.

49
00:02:44,320 --> 00:02:45,280
Not going to happen.

50
00:02:45,600 --> 00:02:46,280
Not going to happen.

51
00:02:47,240 --> 00:02:50,860
Yeah, but we do have that leverage if we were willing to use it,

52
00:02:50,920 --> 00:02:54,400
but it takes political courage to do so.

53
00:02:54,400 --> 00:02:58,820
After the first Gulf War, I watched H.W. Bush and Jim Baker

54
00:02:58,820 --> 00:03:01,380
use the leverage gained in that war.

55
00:03:01,820 --> 00:03:03,200
We restrained Israel.

56
00:03:03,800 --> 00:03:05,120
We put people over there and said,

57
00:03:05,460 --> 00:03:10,560
you will not respond to that Scud missile that just hit outside Tel Aviv

58
00:03:10,560 --> 00:03:12,020
that Saddam Hussein shot at them

59
00:03:12,020 --> 00:03:16,020
because we knew the whole coalition would fall apart if Israel joined the war.

60
00:03:16,140 --> 00:03:19,060
That's how they are a strategic liability big time.

61
00:03:19,060 --> 00:03:25,800
If we're not willing to use the leverage that we have like H.W. Bush did at that time

62
00:03:25,800 --> 00:03:26,960
to bring about Oslo,

63
00:03:27,880 --> 00:03:31,420
this relationship is going nowhere but downhill.

